ger average portfolio size during 2026, as well as the $636 million increase in Change in fair value of MSRs, net.\nThe $636 million increase in Change in fair value of MSRs, net was primarily driven by the increase in Change in valuation model inputs or assumptions for MSRs and related liabilities, partially offset by the Change in fair value of MSR hedge and the Collection/realization of cash flows. The increase in the Change in valuation model inputs or assumptions for MSRs and related liabilities and the decrease in Change in fair value of MSR hedge were primarily due to the increase in interest rates during the third quarter of 2026, compared to a decrease in the same period in 2025. The change in Collection/realization of cash flows was driven by the larger average portfolio size during 2026.\nNine months ended September 30, 2026 summary\n"}
